/Typical Cloud Audit Lifecycle:

    Plan the audit (Define scope, goals)
    Collect information (from both provider and consumer)
    Evaluate and analyze (security posture, compliance)
    Report findings (including any violations or risks)
    Recommend improvements (or verify compliance)    

/Why Cloud Auditing is Important:

    Builds trust between consumer and provider
    Ensures transparency in service delivery
    Helps in achieving regulatory compliance
    Detects vulnerabilities or misconfigurations early

