//summary for cloud deployment models 

| Feature         | **Public Cloud**                                  | **Private Cloud**                                    | **Hybrid Cloud**                                                   | **Community Cloud**                                        |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Ownership**   | Third-party provider                              | Single organization                                  | Combination of private and public                                  | Shared by multiple organizations                           |
| **Access**      | Open to general public / multiple tenants         | Restricted to one organization                       | Private for sensitive workloads, public for others                 | Restricted to members of the community                     |
| **Cost**        | Low upfront cost, pay-as-you-go                   | High upfront cost                                    | Moderate; mix of public pay-as-you-go + private                    | Shared cost among community members                        |
| **Control**     | Limited control                                   | Full control                                         | Control over private part; less control over public                | Shared control among community members                     |
| **Security**    | Moderate; provider-managed                        | High; customizable security                          | High for private part, moderate for public part                    | High; agreed-upon security standards                       |
| **Scalability** | High; easily scalable                             | Limited by in-house resources                        | Scalable for public workloads                                      | Moderate to high depending on community resources          |
| **Compliance**  | May be challenging for strict regulations         | Easier to meet regulatory requirements               | Can comply using private part                                      | Easier if standards agreed within the community            |
| **Maintenance** | Managed by provider                               | Managed internally                                   | Split between internal team and provider                           | Managed by community or designated provider                |
| **Best For**    | Startups, small businesses, fluctuating workloads | Enterprises with sensitive data or strict compliance | Organizations needing both flexibility and control                 | Organizations with shared goals or regulatory requirements |
| **Examples**    | AWS, Azure, Google Cloud                          | Internal private cloud, hosted private cloud         | Banking apps: sensitive data on private, public apps for customers | Government departments, research collaborations            |

Public Cloud → Cost-effective, scalable, low control
Private Cloud → High security, full control, higher cost
Hybrid Cloud → Combines best of public and private, flexible
Community Cloud → Shared infrastructure for organizations with common requirements

